---
source: crates/instrukt-cli/tests/cases/harness.rs
expression: help
---
Install, remove, inspect and run instrukt's git hook sections

Usage: instrukt hooks <COMMAND>

Commands:
  install  Write instrukt's section into each hook file it uses, in the hooks directory
           `core.hooksPath` names or the repository's own. Touches no line outside the section
  remove   Remove instrukt's section from every hook file; every other line and the files themselves
           remain
  status   Per hook: the hooks directory, whether the section is current, outdated or absent (with
           the line to give a hook manager), and the last run's outcome
  run      What a section calls: pre-commit stages a project layer converted to the current schema
           into the commit; checkout waits for entrypoint rendering and first publication if needed;
           other publication triggers run detached. Never fails the git operation
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version
